  :title "Marshal with the Closures flag"
  :kind :design
  :why "closures marshal as code pointers and digests of the program; oi's closures are Go values (lib-marshal/intext and intext_par, run since the C API on ci gives their stubs: doc/ocaml/OCAML-SURVEY.md, \"As built: the C API on ci\") Since OC216 (a) (the user 2026-11-10; OT7 (a) reversed): a closure marshals as a block of Closure_tag whose first field is a code pointer, the number of its code (oi's) or its class (the AOT runtime's) in the process's table with the digest of its name, its free variables after it; read back in the same program it is the closure again. Left: none at oi's level and the light AOT level; a program that reads a closure another process wrote"
  :decided "O7, OC103; OT7 (a), the user 2026-11-05; OC216 (a)"
  :match [#"^fail known marshal: "]}
 {:id :speed
  :title "speed: programs beyond the check's limit"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "an interpreter of Lambda over Go values is one or two orders of magnitude slower than ocamlc's bytecode on loops of 10^8 or 10^9 steps; the check's limit is OI_TIMEOUT (120 s); the programs are named in oi-slow.edn. Deferred, not by design (OC196 (a)): no rule makes speed part of the language; owned by the AOT level and oi's speed work"
  :decided "OC65; OC196 (a), the user 2026-11-09"
  :match [#"^slow timeout "]}
]
